WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.600
SLOT makes time for independent sports coaches and their clients. This is a captioned walkthrough

00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:09.200
using real application screenshots and fictional demonstration data.

00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:14.200
Choose an individual or group session. The summary shows the studio timezone, duration, price and

00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:19.200
available places. A reservation holds a place for ten minutes.

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:24.400
Confirm the simulated payment and the booking becomes confirmed. No money changes hands in this

00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:29.600
demonstration. A signed Stripe test webhook is a separate optional integration.

00:00:29.600 --> 00:00:34.800
Two clients request the last place through the real booking service. One succeeds. The other

00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:40.000
receives a clear conflict message. Transactions and database rules protect capacity.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:44.400
The coach manages sessions, services, working hours and absences. Clients can move or cancel their

00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:48.800
own bookings. Server permissions enforce these boundaries.

00:00:48.800 --> 00:00:54.800
Next.js, TypeScript and PostgreSQL power the application. GitHub checks exercise booking and browser journeys. External

00:00:54.800 --> 00:01:00.800
payment and email delivery still require provider testing. Explore the code and its documented tradeoffs.
